---
// Hero layer A (PRD §5.2): the RISHI wordmark and its scroll dissolve. Split
// out of Hero.astro for the CLAUDE.md §5 line cap. Hero.astro owns the section
// and the subject; this file owns everything about the letters.
//
// Rendered as inline SVG rather than a text node, because only textLength can
// pin the glyphs to an exact width at every viewport. The visually hidden <h1>
// carries the semantics while the SVG does the typography.
//
// The viewBox is the glyphs' painted ink box, measured off a real render
// rather than taken from font metrics (getBBox and getExtentOfChar both report
// advance boxes, which are wider and much taller than the paint). Cropping to
// it is what removes the dead space around the letters, so the capped width
// below is all glyph. preserveAspectRatio stays at the default so the
// letterforms scale uniformly, and lengthAdjust="spacing" only redistributes
// the gaps between glyphs — never the letters themselves.
---

{/* Sticky so it dissolves in place. data-wordmark is the script hook. */}
<div class="wordmark-wrap" data-wordmark>
  <h1 class="visually-hidden">Rishi</h1>
  <svg
    class="wordmark"
    viewBox="63 31 2055 735"
    preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
    aria-hidden="true"
    focusable="false"
  >
    <text
      x="0"
      y="748"
      textLength="2146"
      lengthAdjust="spacing"
      dominant-baseline="alphabetic">RISHI</text
    >
  </svg>
</div>

<script>
  import { runHeroDissolveFallback } from "../scripts/hero-dissolve";

  runHeroDissolveFallback();
</script>

<style>
  /* Sticky wrapper spans the viewport; the SVG inside it is centred and capped,
     pinned just under the nav so the head and shoulders cross the lower half of
     the letters. grid-area places it in the hero's single cell, under the
     subject (z-index 2, Hero.astro). */
  .wordmark-wrap {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    height: 100dvh;
    /* Overflow stays visible so the dissolve's 8px blur is not clipped;
       .hero already clips anything that leaves the section. */
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + 0.5rem);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .wordmark {
    display: block;
    /* 72vw centred: ~14% margin each side at 1440px. Sits between the original
       22vw type and the edge-to-edge version. */
    width: clamp(320px, 72vw, 1100px);
    margin-inline: auto;
    /* Ratio matches the ink-box viewBox, so width drives height and the glyphs
       are never stretched. */
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 2055 / 735;
  }

  .wordmark text {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    /* 1000px type with the baseline at y=748 puts the caps inside the viewBox
       above; textLength then pins the advance to the box width. */
    font-size: 1000px;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    fill: var(--heading);
  }

  /* --- Scroll dissolve over the first 40% (PRD 5.2) ---------------------- */
  /* Animated on the wrapper, never the SVG, so the glyphs stay crisp at rest:
     no filter or transform touches the SVG at scroll position 0. */
  /* Starts at 0.01% rather than 0% so the resting frame keeps filter:none and
     transform:none — a blur(0) layer would soften the glyph edges at rest. */
  @keyframes wordmark-dissolve {
    0% {
      opacity: 1;
      filter: none;
      transform: none;
    }
    0.01% {
      opacity: 1;
      filter: blur(0);
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
    100% {
      opacity: 0;
      filter: blur(8px);
      transform: translateY(-8%);
    }
  }

  @supports (animation-timeline: scroll()) {
    /* Longhands, never the `animation` shorthand: if the timeline is allowed to
       fold into it, the minifier emits `animation: ... scroll(root)` and every
       browser drops the declaration, silently killing the dissolve. The
       :where() prefix keeps this rule from merging with the one below. */
    :where([data-wordmark]).wordmark-wrap {
      animation-name: wordmark-dissolve;
      animation-duration: 1ms; /* Overridden by the timeline. */
      animation-timing-function: linear;
      animation-fill-mode: both;
    }

    .wordmark-wrap {
      animation-timeline: scroll(root block);
      animation-range: 0 40dvh;
    }
  }

  /* Script fallback drives the same visuals from --hero-progress. */
  .wordmark-wrap[data-fallback="on"] {
    opacity: calc(1 - var(--hero-progress, 0));
    filter: blur(calc(var(--hero-progress, 0) * 8px));
    transform: translateY(calc(var(--hero-progress, 0) * -8%));
  }

  /* 640px rather than the project's usual 768px: below this the 72vw cap makes
     the wordmark too small to carry the composition, so it goes near-full-bleed. */
  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .wordmark {
      width: 88vw;
    }

    /* Pushed further down than on desktop: the mobile wordmark is short, so the
       figure has to reach well up into it for the overlap to read. */
    .wordmark-wrap {
      padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + 16dvh);
    }
  }

  /* --- Reduced motion: opacity only, no blur or movement ----------------- */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    @keyframes wordmark-dissolve {
      from {
        opacity: 1;
      }
      to {
        opacity: 0;
      }
    }

    .wordmark-wrap[data-fallback="on"] {
      filter: none;
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
